<title>SPAIN: Spain's Tabacalera posts 4.1 pct fall in 96 profit.</title>
<headline>Spain's Tabacalera posts 4.1 pct fall in 96 profit.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full 1996 results for Spain's Tabacalera in billions of pesetas, unless stated:</p>
<p> Attributable		   13.46	     vs     14.03</p>
<p> Net profit		     13.30	     vs     13.80</p>
<p> Pretaxed profit		18.21	     vs     18.87</p>
<p> Turnover net		  329.08	     vs    334.53</p>
<p> Tobacco, stamps sales net of tax     817.73  vs    779.10</p>
<p> Net income				   335.56  vs    344.63</p>
<p> Operating costs			    322.92  vs    326.52</p>
<p> Operating profit			    12.65  vs     18.11</p>
<p> Ordinary profit			     17.70  vs     23.67</p>
<p> Financial results			    2.46  vs	2.24</p>
<p> Extraordinary profit			 0.51  vs     (4.80)</p>
<p>NOTE - Tabacalera added in a note that it would continue a strategy of specialisation in three business area -- cigars, cigarettes and retail distribution.</p>
<p>It would also continue to seek a further degree of internationalisation.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
